# 82 MB of raw NOAA, SPC and FEMA downloads, and 31 MB of built Parquet. Rebuilt from
# source.lock.json and reference.lock.json, never committed.
#
# The two directories are named separately rather than ignoring data/ outright. DVC
# works by putting a tracked pointer file NEXT TO the untracked data, so a blanket
# data/ rule makes data/parquet.dvc git-ignored and dvc add refuses to write it.
#
# data/parquet is NOT here, and that is deliberate. The release is tracked as seven
# DVC outputs rather than one directory, so each artifact's pointer sits beside it
# inside data/parquet/ and `dvc add` writes data/parquet/.gitignore naming the seven
# data directories. Letting dvc own that file is the only arrangement of the three
# tried that works, and the other two fail in different ways.
#
# A blanket `data/parquet/` rule makes the pointers git-ignored and `dvc add` refuses
# outright with `bad DVC file name ... is git-ignored`. A negation does not rescue it,
# because git will not re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded.
#
# `data/parquet/*/` passes that test and fails silently, which is worse. The pointers
# are visible to git and INVISIBLE TO DVC. A bare `dvc push` then prints `Everything
# is up to date` and exits 0 having pushed nothing, and `dvc status` says there is no
# data tracked in the project at all. Naming a pointer explicitly still works, so the
# pointers are fine and only discovery is broken. Reproduced in a three file scratch
# repo before this comment was written.
data/raw/
data/tiles/
data/labelstudio/
# Contact sheets for the labelling pass. Generated from the tiles, which are not here
# either, and they are an annotation aid rather than part of the release.
data/sheets/
!data/*.dvc

# The DVC cache is a second copy of the Parquet. The local remote is a third.
/.dvc/cache/
/.dvc/tmp/
/dvc-remote/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
# dagster dev leaves run storage behind
.dagster_home/
dagster_home/
tmp*/
